<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Tamil strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  Tamil iOS uses native words and bare verbs on buttons ("சேமி", "நீக்கு"); sentences use the polite "-ங்கள்".
  Migraine is "ஒற்றைத் தலைவலி"; a migraine day is "தாக்குதல் நாள்" (attack day), because the migraine word has 14 characters.
  Tamil has the CLDR plural forms one and other. The duration chips have no unit; the captions name the hours.
-->
